comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-18T15:02:14.482Z","harness:codex","Red-first evidence: the new Vitest reporter made the otherwise-green 22-test MCP integration suite exit 1 for full on update, dep on deps, and dryRun on test-all. Removed the inert inputs and retained dedicated negative warning tests with exact allowlist identities. Production warning compatibility is unchanged."
  "2026-09-18T15:13:29.199Z","harness:codex","Integration repair preserves real coverage: compact update changes priority and asserts persisted state without inert full; deps observes the edge established by update without inert dep; test-all executes its real contract without inert dryRun. Runtime advisory behavior remains unchanged. CI reporter allows only the exact existing negative read-mutation test and two declared warning identities. Unattributed or changed identities fail. A real nested Vitest process proves passing assertions cannot hide a warning failure."
  "2026-09-18T15:30:18.720Z","harness:codex","Pre-PR self-review found the coverage-shard workflow overrides the configured reporters. Red-first real runner control confirmed --reporter=default incorrectly exited zero despite an undeclared-option warning, and the shard dispatch unit test showed the gate missing. The sandbox runner now appends the mandatory reporter whenever CLI reporters replace the config list, including split and equals syntax. The real otherwise-green child-process negative control exercises this override path."
  "2026-09-18T16:12:23.292Z","harness:codex",Final complete 9011-test suite and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage pass with the mandatory MCP reporter enabled. This includes real subprocess reporter-override negative control and corrected integration consumers. No coverage exclusions or warning exemptions were broadened.
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-18T15:15:15.022Z","harness:codex",A passing assertion does not prove a supplied option was consumed. Repository MCP tests require both mutation/result assertions and diagnostic conformance. Narrow negative-test exemptions must bind the complete file/test/option/tool/action identity; a real child runner is needed to prove a reporter failure changes the process exit status.
